# Rule 39 — Redesign phase PRs must include the phase checklist

## Why this rule exists

PRs #175–#178 shipped staged implementation of the redesign. Reviewers cannot verify what was done, what remains in the current phase, or what sits in a later phase unless the PR description says so. The old status file has left the repository; the PR description is the record.

## What you must do for every redesign-phase PR

Include this block in the PR description:

```
## Redesign phase status

### Phase X — <name> (this PR)
- [x] …completed item…
- [ ] …remaining item still in this phase…

### Next phase — <name>
- [ ] …first item planned for the next phase…
```

- Mark an item done only when it is fully implemented. Scaffolding is not done.
- Name any scope discovered during implementation that belongs in the same phase.
- Leave intentionally deferred items listed as remaining.

Before requesting review, confirm the PR body contains that block.

## Scope

This rule applies when the branch, commit, or PR refers to a redesign phase, or you are asked to continue one.
